WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.717 --> 00:00:16.243
"What you talking about?"

2
00:00:16.644 --> 00:00:18.364
Maggie asked Henry in surprise.

3
00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:22.587
"I thought we agreed that Kyle was our top suspect."

4
00:00:23.607 --> 00:00:25.228
"He was," Henry said.

5
00:00:25.248 --> 00:00:27.449
"But he's not anymore.

6
00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:31.892
He just told us that he didn't know Cole was interested in frogs.

7
00:00:32.924 --> 00:00:36.447
That means he wouldn't know that Cole would be blamed for the prank!"

8
00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:40.290
"I didn't think of that," Maggie said.

9
00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:47.396
"Plus it would be stupid for Kyle to use grape sports drink for the ant prank," Henry added.

10
00:00:47.416 --> 00:00:51.099
"Everyone saw him drinking it all day."

11
00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:53.080
Maggie shrugged.

12
00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.622
"Maybe he's not very bright.

13
00:00:56.723 --> 00:01:00.326
Or maybe he was lying about not knowing Cole liked frogs."

14
00:01:02.067 --> 00:01:03.541
"Maybe," Henry said.

15
00:01:03.561 --> 00:01:05.862
"But I don't think so.

16
00:01:06.963 --> 00:01:08.984
We'd better check out our other suspects.

17
00:01:10.205 --> 00:01:11.146
Starting with Tommy.

18
00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:16.309
He definitely knew Cole liked frogs because of his parents' pet store.

19
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:19.752
Plus Tommy could have gotten the frogs there."

20
00:01:19.772 --> 00:01:22.434
"Sure," Maggie said.

21
00:01:22.454 --> 00:01:26.376
"But Cole isn't the only one who's a better swimmer than Tommy.

22
00:01:27.857 --> 00:01:31.080
Why didn't Tommy try to ruin Daisy and Kyle's chances too?"

23
00:01:32.356 --> 00:01:35.638
"Maybe that's why Tommy did the ant prank," Henry said.

24
00:01:35.658 --> 00:01:39.701
"He was trying to get rid of the other two swimmers that way.

25
00:01:40.842 --> 00:01:44.845
If Daisy got bitten by ants, she might not want to try out anymore.

26
00:01:45.806 --> 00:01:49.268
And using grape sports drink meant Kyle might get the blame."

27
00:01:50.809 --> 00:01:51.750
Maggie gasped.

28
00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:54.352
"Henry, you're a genius!"

29
00:01:54.832 --> 00:01:55.612
she exclaimed.

30
00:01:55.632 --> 00:01:58.194
"That makes perfect sense!

31
00:01:59.335 --> 00:02:00.396
Let's go tell the coach!"

32
00:02:01.564 --> 00:02:03.405
"Hold on," Henry said.

33
00:02:03.425 --> 00:02:05.626
"It's just a theory.

34
00:02:06.666 --> 00:02:08.087
We haven't proven anything yet."

35
00:02:08.107 --> 00:02:10.728
"How are we going to prove it?"

36
00:02:11.048 --> 00:02:11.828
Maggie asked.

37
00:02:11.848 --> 00:02:13.989
"I'm not sure yet.

38
00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:16.410
Let's go talk to Tommy."

39
00:02:17.871 --> 00:02:19.392
Henry looked over at the pool.

40
00:02:20.612 --> 00:02:23.053
Most of the swimmers were chasing the last few frogs.

41
00:02:24.154 --> 00:02:25.254
Lauren was watching them.

42
00:02:26.314 --> 00:02:29.676
Coach Phillips seemed to be counting the frogs that were already in the buckets.

43
00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:32.325
But Tommy was nowhere in sight.

44
00:02:32.345 --> 00:02:34.125
"Where is he?"

45
00:02:34.526 --> 00:02:35.226
Maggie wondered.

46
00:02:35.246 --> 00:02:38.207
"I don't know," Henry said.

47
00:02:38.227 --> 00:02:40.608
"But there's his brother John.

48
00:02:41.709 --> 00:02:43.829
Let's go ask him if he knows where Tommy is."

49
00:02:44.870 --> 00:02:46.390
John was climbing out of the pool.

50
00:02:47.391 --> 00:02:49.512
He had an annoyed expression on his face.

51
00:02:50.632 --> 00:02:53.573
Henry wondered if that was because tryouts had been disrupted again.

52
00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.495
Everyone in town knew that John was a very talented swimmer.

53
00:02:57.515 --> 00:03:00.577
"Hi, John," Henry said.

54
00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:03.139
"We're looking for your brother.

55
00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:04.960
Where did he go?"

56
00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.242
"That's a good question."

57
00:03:08.183 --> 00:03:10.164
John looked more annoyed than ever.

58
00:03:10.184 --> 00:03:13.027
"I was just looking for him myself."

59
00:03:13.047 --> 00:03:15.909
"Why?" Maggie asked.

60
00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:22.834
"Tryouts will start again in a few minutes, and he needs all the practice he can get," John

61
00:03:22.915 --> 00:03:27.138
said. "Tommy isn't taking these tryouts very seriously."

62
00:03:28.139 --> 00:03:29.440
Then he stomped away.

63
00:03:30.544 --> 00:03:31.685
Maggie watched him go.

64
00:03:31.705 --> 00:03:35.148
"John sounded mad," she said.

65
00:03:35.168 --> 00:03:38.690
"And did you hear what he said about Tommy?

66
00:03:39.771 --> 00:03:42.713
Maybe John suspects his brother of causing all the trouble!"

67
00:03:43.754 --> 00:03:44.575
Henry shrugged.

68
00:03:44.595 --> 00:03:47.757
"Brothers get mad at each other all the time.

69
00:03:48.858 --> 00:03:52.921
John is probably just embarrassed because his brother is a terrible swimmer."

70
00:03:52.941 --> 00:03:56.904
"Yeah, you're probably right," Maggie agreed.

71
00:03:58.316 --> 00:04:01.218
Henry noticed Cole putting another frog in one of the buckets.

72
00:04:02.479 --> 00:04:06.141
Most of the other swimmers were climbing out of the pool and grabbing their towels.

73
00:04:06.161 --> 00:04:10.044
"It looks like they caught all the frogs," Henry said.

74
00:04:10.064 --> 00:04:14.627
"We'd better hurry if we want to talk to Tommy before tryouts start again."

75
00:04:14.647 --> 00:04:16.608
"There's Daisy.

76
00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:20.111
Let's ask her if she's seen him," Maggie said.

77
00:04:24.614 --> 00:04:29.629
saw Tommy heading toward the pool building a few minutes ago," Daisy told them a second later.

78
00:04:29.649 --> 00:04:33.410
"He probably went inside to use the bathroom."

79
00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.931
"Thanks," Henry said.

80
00:04:36.972 --> 00:04:39.493
He wondered if he should ask Daisy more questions.

81
00:04:40.753 --> 00:04:42.314
She was still a suspect too.

82
00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:45.135
"Hey, Daisy," he said.

83
00:04:45.155 --> 00:04:50.418
"When Lauren made you jog, did you make it around the building first?"

84
00:04:51.598 --> 00:04:52.719
Daisy smiled.

85
00:04:52.739 --> 00:04:55.740
"Not this time," she said.

86
00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.858
"At first I was keeping up with Cole, Kyle, and John.

87
00:05:00.879 --> 00:05:06.283
But then I saw a pretty flower growing beside the running trail, and I stopped to look at

88
00:05:06.343 --> 00:05:10.526
it. I thought I might want to come back and paint it later.

89
00:05:11.727 --> 00:05:14.409
So I was one of the last ones to make it back."

90
00:05:14.429 --> 00:05:19.072
"Oh." Henry remembered that Daisy liked art.

91
00:05:20.093 --> 00:05:22.434
He'd seen some of her paintings displayed at school.

92
00:05:23.495 --> 00:05:24.596
Daisy walked away.

93
00:05:25.612 --> 00:05:28.054
"Why were you asking her about jogging?"

94
00:05:28.514 --> 00:05:29.574
Maggie asked Henry.

95
00:05:29.594 --> 00:05:33.377
"I thought we were in a hurry to talk to Tommy."

96
00:05:33.397 --> 00:05:38.960
"I'm still trying to figure out who dumped those frogs the second time," Henry said.

97
00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:43.803
"It had to be the first person who got back from that jog.

98
00:05:44.983 --> 00:05:47.585
So Daisy's probably not our culprit."

99
00:05:49.086 --> 00:05:50.547
"I could have told you that!"

100
00:05:51.487 --> 00:05:52.548
Maggie rolled her eyes.

101
00:05:53.696 --> 00:05:56.179
"Our top suspect is Tommy now, remember?"

102
00:05:56.199 --> 00:05:59.644
"Okay. Let's go find him."

103
00:06:00.685 --> 00:06:03.909
Before they could move, Henry and Maggie heard an angry howl.

104
00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.812
"Hey!" Kyle yelled.

105
00:06:08.656 --> 00:06:10.398
"Someone poured paint in my gym bag!"
